{"id": "EUVD-2026-82008", "enisaUuid": "51a1b0b6-cf6a-3cae-b841-76a47cdccc20", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: ptrace: Keep 'orig_x0' in-sync with x0 on syscall entry\n\nCommit e057b9477232 (\"arm64: syscall: Ensure saved x0 is kept in-sync\nwith tracer updates\") attempted to resolve a long-standing issue with\nsyscall entry tracing, where a tracer is able to manipulate the first\nsyscall argument without being subjected to seccomp or audit checking.\n\nUnfortunately, that fix was incomplete [1], as it failed to update\n'orig_x0' between a tracer updating x0 during a seccomp ptrace exit\n(SECCOMP_RET_TRACE) and the seccomp filter being re-evaluated.\n\nRather than add hooks to the core seccomp code, instead move the\nsynchronisation code into the ptrace GPR and syscall setting code so\nthat 'orig_x0' is kept up to date with x0 whenever we're stopped on the\nsyscall entry path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:12", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/332c9c1a148d0425326989c1187face8f6b2a60c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce17c651a90e242ad48df0df89b1e4cebcda5e14", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9e2854fcff5733ffc607e8ecc87e0e591ab41fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f433869f23841a50455c4087d85540d5b4d37cde", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88b839ce497ccb1ff92f7ae742c78dd2937ba572"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90347", "GHSA-rg84-frxc-rfcx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f594906-7784-3360-aba8-b08e20ac97ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cd110cb8369d6b37ef5ccfe56b3fa1338c9615 <e9e2854fcff5733ffc607e8ecc87e0e591ab41fd"}, {"id": "277813ae-d601-3d98-8bec-7b56dd818193", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cd110cb8369d6b37ef5ccfe56b3fa1338c9615 <88b839ce497ccb1ff92f7ae742c78dd2937ba572"}, {"id": "32b61f4a-1567-3d6a-bf66-1147cec8616e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "62b53936-eac0-355c-a8ea-909339f1549b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "648bab43-62a3-33d7-b3f4-68473b6012c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cd110cb8369d6b37ef5ccfe56b3fa1338c9615 <ce17c651a90e242ad48df0df89b1e4cebcda5e14"}, {"id": "773296f2-15da-3df5-a949-2a3be4ac2949", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7a22fc27-fc22-34c6-852b-91722dbe64d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "9373cfec-9683-3bf7-a783-a7aa4f4ee935", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b8ece50d-773d-39f7-b95e-9d8e11d13e6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "ba76eb64-ca61-37f8-9914-f23ded0e8463", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "c5a36853-31ec-338a-898d-88d2c999c286", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cd110cb8369d6b37ef5ccfe56b3fa1338c9615 <332c9c1a148d0425326989c1187face8f6b2a60c"}, {"id": "df08f058-7ad7-3e2f-b27f-633a91fc32c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5cd110cb8369d6b37ef5ccfe56b3fa1338c9615 <f433869f23841a50455c4087d85540d5b4d37cde"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f8d7eee6-47b1-3c1d-ac54-4bdc1e4b3548", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}